      "body": "Coordination: deferring to @auser's #386 — it covers this issue's scope (schema-2 default-off term, sweep flag, w=1.0 measurement) and the #364 entropy-collapse analysis establishes the sharper conclusion that the binding constraint is the proposal mechanism, not the acceptance filter. Unassigning per the assignment=active convention.\n\nOne supplementary datum still in flight on our side, posted here when it lands with clear labeling: a **w=4.0** sweep arm from an independent implementation whose estimator references the **parent's own distribution** (children-vs-parent) rather than the global prior — it answers 'does a much stronger veto-side weight move the frontier at all,' which the w=1.0 result leaves open. If it also leaves the frontier unmoved, that closes the veto-side question from both directions and the proposal-mechanism conclusion stands unqualified.",
