      "body": "Supplementary datum, closing the veto-side question from the strong end (promised above): an independent implementation of this issue's term — estimator referenced to the **parent's own distribution** (children-vs-parent) rather than the global prior — swept the same 9-point grid under probability/contrast at **w = 1.0 and w = 4.0**. Both arms: **all nine rows identical to the unweighted sweep, to the digit** (top-1, bits, regions, per point). Combined with #386's w=1.0 global-reference measurement: two estimator references × two weight scales, zero split decisions changed. The acceptance-side lever is exhausted; the #364 proposal-mechanism conclusion stands unqualified — distinctiveness has to come from what the clustering is given to propose from, not from how proposals are scored.",
